 "sections": [
  {
   "name": "Why Your Car Does Not Bounce",
   "lines": [
    [
     "c05_1",
     {
      "label": "hook",
      "head": "Why your car *doesn't bounce*",
      "pose": "point",
      "face": "grin",
      "prop": {
       "type": "suspension",
       "mode": "good"
      }
     },
     "Hit a bump in a car, and it barely moves. Here is why."
    ],
    [
     "c05_2",
     {
      "label": "springs",
      "head": "*Springs* soak up the bump",
      "pose": "present",
      "face": "smile",
      "prop": {
       "type": "suspension",
       "mode": "spring",
       "label": "SPRING ONLY"
      }
     },
     "Springs between the wheel and the body compress over a bump, so the body does not get the full hit."
    ],
    [
     "c05_3",
     {
      "label": "problem",
      "head": "But springs keep *bouncing*",
      "pose": "shrug",
      "face": "worried",
      "prop": {
       "type": "suspension",
       "mode": "none",
       "label": "BOING BOING"
      }
     },
     "On their own, springs would keep bouncing after every bump, like a pogo stick."
    ],
    [
     "c05_4",
     {
      "label": "dampers",
      "head": "*Shock absorbers* calm it down",
      "pose": "present",
      "face": "smug",
      "prop": {
       "type": "suspension",
       "mode": "good",
       "label": "SPRING + DAMPER"
      }
     },
     "Shock absorbers, or dampers, force oil through tiny holes. That turns the bounce into heat, and the car settles at once."
    ],
    [
     "c05_5",
     {
      "label": "real job",
      "head": "The real job: *grip*",
      "pose": "count",
      "face": "smile",
      "prop": {
       "type": "checklist",
       "items": [
        [
         "Tyres stay on the road",
         true
        ],
        [
         "Steering stays sharp",
         true
        ],
        [
         "Shorter stopping",
         true
        ]
       ]
      }
     },
     "The real job is not comfort. It keeps the tyres pressed onto the road, so you can steer and brake."
    ],
    [
     "c05_6",
     {
      "label": "worn",
      "head": "Worn shocks are *dangerous*",
      "pose": "shy",
      "face": "worried",
      "prop": {
       "type": "versus",
       "a": {
        "t": "GOOD SHOCKS",
        "big": "planted",
        "sub": "tyres stay down"
       },
       "b": {
        "t": "WORN SHOCKS",
        "big": "floaty",
        "sub": "longer stops"
       },
       "win": "a"
      }
     },
     "Worn dampers can make your stopping distance longer, and make the car wallow and float over bumps."
    ],
    [
     "c05_7",
     {
      "label": "test",
      "head": "Try the *bounce test*",
      "pose": "present",
      "face": "grin",
      "prop": {
       "type": "suspension",
       "mode": "good"
      }
     },
     "Push down hard on one corner and let go. If it bounces more than once or twice, get your shocks checked."
    ],
    [
     "c05_8",
     {
      "label": "takeaway",
      "head": "Springs hold, dampers *control*",
      "pose": "thumbs",
      "face": "happy",
      "prop": {
       "type": "tags",
       "items": [
        "SPRINGS",
        "DAMPERS",
        "GRIP"
       ]
      }
     },
     "Springs hold the car up. Dampers control the bounce. Together, they keep you on the road."
    ]
   ]
